  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR Global Health Research Unit on Respiratory Health (RESPIRE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To build on their track-record of epidemiological research and capacity development in LMIC. 2) To invest in and strengthen our existing collaborations with leading research groups in South Asia. 3) To leverage their critical mass in respiratory, informatics and health services research, to expand efforts into the neglected field of applied respiratory research. 4) Build a network of laboratories and experts across strategically important countries from which to expand to similar local contexts elsewhere.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A UK and low- and middle-income country (LMIC) partnership that aims to improve respiratory outcomes from common respiratory communicable and non-communicable disorders. This research has the direct and primary aim of improving the health, wellbeing and economic development of people in LMICs.</narrative>
  </description>
